docs {
  # Create Certification
  
  Creates a new certification block for your profile. This endpoint uses the batch update system, so you can create multiple certifications in a single request.
  
  ## Request Body
  
  The request uses the batch update format with a `creations` array. Each creation object contains:
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `block_type` | string | ✅ | Must be `"certification"` |
  | `section_name` | string | ❌ | Section name (e.g., "certifications", "credentials") |
  | `sort_order` | number | ❌ | Order within section (0 = first) |
  | `data` | object | ✅ | Certification data (see below) |
  
  ### Certification Data Fields
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `name` | string | ✅ | Certification name (max 255 chars) |
  | `issuing_organization` | string | ✅ | Organization that issued the certification (max 255 chars) |
  | `organization_url` | string | ❌ | Issuing organization's website URL |
  | `credential_id` | string | ❌ | Certification/credential ID or license number |
  | `credential_url` | string | ❌ | URL to verify the credential (e.g., verification page) |
  | `issue_date` | string | ❌ | Issue date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format |
  | `expiration_date` | string | ❌ | Expiration date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format |
  | `does_not_expire` | boolean | ❌ | Whether the certification never expires (default: `false`) |
  
  ## Example: Certification with Expiration
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "certification",
        "section_name": "certifications",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "Google Cloud Professional Cloud Architect",
          "issuing_organization": "Google Cloud",
          "organization_url": "https://cloud.google.com",
          "credential_id": "GCP-PCA-123456",
          "credential_url": "https://www.credential.net/verify",
          "issue_date": "2023-03-20",
          "expiration_date": "2025-03-20",
          "does_not_expire": false
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Certification Without Expiration
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "certification",
        "section_name": "certifications",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "Certified Kubernetes Administrator",
          "issuing_organization": "Cloud Native Computing Foundation",
          "organization_url": "https://www.cncf.io",
          "credential_id": "CKA-123456",
          "credential_url": "https://www.cncf.io/certification/cka",
          "issue_date": "2022-11-10",
          "does_not_expire": true
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Professional License
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "certification",
        "section_name": "certifications",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "Professional Engineer License",
          "issuing_organization": "State Board of Professional Engineers",
          "organization_url": "https://stateboard.example.gov",
          "credential_id": "PE-12345",
          "issue_date": "2020-06-15",
          "expiration_date": "2024-06-15",
          "does_not_expire": false
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Multiple Certifications
  
  You can create multiple certifications in a single request:
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "certification",
        "section_name": "certifications",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "AWS Certified Developer",
          "issuing_organization": "Amazon Web Services",
          "organization_url": "https://aws.amazon.com",
          "credential_id": "AWS-DEV-789",
          "issue_date": "2023-01-10",
          "expiration_date": "2026-01-10",
          "does_not_expire": false
        }
      },
      {
        "block_type": "certification",
        "section_name": "certifications",
        "sort_order": 1,
        "data": {
          "name": "Microsoft Azure Fundamentals",
          "issuing_organization": "Microsoft",
          "organization_url": "https://azure.microsoft.com",
          "credential_id": "AZ-900-123456",
          "credential_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/verify",
          "issue_date": "2022-08-05",
          "expiration_date": null,
          "does_not_expire": true
        }
      },
      {
        "block_type": "certification",
        "section_name": "certifications",
        "sort_order": 2,
        "data": {
          "name": "Certified Scrum Master",
          "issuing_organization": "Scrum Alliance",
          "organization_url": "https://www.scrumalliance.org",
          "credential_id": "CSM-456789",
          "issue_date": "2021-05-20",
          "expiration_date": "2023-05-20",
          "does_not_expire": false
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Minimal Certification Entry
  
  Only `name` and `issuing_organization` are required:
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "certification",
        "section_name": "certifications",
        "data": {
          "name": "First Aid Certification",
          "issuing_organization": "Red Cross"
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Response (200 OK)
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Version updated successfully",
    "data": {
      "version": {
        "id": 9,
        "version_number": 9,
        "created_at": "2024-01-16T15:00:00Z"
      },
      "created_blocks": [105],
      "updated_blocks": [],
      "deleted_blocks": []
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  
  - Both `name` and `issuing_organization` are required fields
  - Dates must be in `YYYY-MM-DD` format
  - If `does_not_expire` is `true`, `expiration_date` should be `null` or omitted
  - `credential_id` and `credential_url` are useful for verification purposes
  - Common certification types include: cloud platforms, programming languages, project management, security, etc.
  - Each request creates a new version, preserving history
}

